update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'| P1 – B4.1/B4.2/B4.3/B4.4/B4.5/B4.6 (Chapter 2)                                       | Adopt the scenario-based EOC structure, alternates, roster, liaison desks, job action sheets and welfare arrangements.                                                                                          | CDRRMO Head / EOC Manager                                                                    | HRMO; partner offices; cluster leads; OCD VIII                       | Approved roster/designations, alternates, job action sheets, welfare and shift plans.                            |\n| P2 – A2.5 / B4.3 (Chapter 2)                                                         | Formalise routine 24-hour duty roster, shift handover and distinct task streams in the existing OpCen arrangement.                                                                                              | CDRRMO Head / Operations and Warning                                                         | HRMO; City Traffic; Public Safety; Emergency Monitoring              | Approved duty SOP, roster, handover records, staffing gap analysis and review.                                   |\n| P2 – B2–B7 (Chapter 1 scope map for Chapter 6)                                       | Coordinate Chapter 4 operational requirements with Chapter 6 EOC information management, logistics, resource requests, communications, situation reporting and Geo-COP without duplicating those detailed SOPs. | CDRRMO Head / EOC Manager                                                                    | EOC sections; GIS/data custodian; Logistics; ICT; sector offices     | Chapter cross-reference, shared forms, data dictionary and tested integrated workflow.                           |\n| P2 – C-interface indicators (Part C ownership; exact rows to verify)                 | Confirm cross-office warning, transport, health, education, utilities, social protection and critical facility interfaces with named focal persons and continuity arrangements.                                 | Each sector office for its statutory function; City Administrator coordination as designated | CDRRMO; CPDO; CSWDO; CHO; Engineering; DepEd; utilities; barangays   | Signed focal-person/coordination register, MOA/issuances where needed, contact tests and documented plan inputs. |\n\n| VALIDATION NOTE. Owners, targets and status are copied from the IAT v1.7 Action Plan (8 November 2026) in Annex 4-A without change; the workbook stays the controlled source. Targets such as "Jan 2027 (with MOP)" are the workbook entries, confirmed there for B1.1, B1.2, B1.3, B1.4, B1.5, A6.2, A6.3, A6.7 and A8.8. This draft is an operational chapter, not an approved local issuance. |\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n\n# 18. Forms, Registers and Annexes\n\nThe following forms are proposed to operationalise the chapter. They shall be configured as controlled forms and cross-referenced to approved protocol steps in the Library and the platform. Fields requiring sensitive personal information shall be held only in authorised restricted records, not in general-purpose EOC forms.\n\n**Table 4.37**\n\n*Forms, Registers and Annexes, With the MODE Form Used for Each*\n\n| **Form / annex code** | **Title**                                              | **Purpose / key fields**                                                                                         | **Primary user / custodian**                        | **MODE form**      |\n|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|--------------------|\n| EWR-F01               | Official warning receipt and verification log          | Source, product ID, issue/receipt time, validity, hazard, area, verification, supersession and escalation.       | Duty officer / Operations and Warning               | EOC-WARN-01        |\n| EWR-F02               | Warning-to-action matrix                               | Hazard, scenario, authoritative trigger, authority, action, target group, channel, acknowledgement and review.   | CDRRMO / contingency plan owner                     | Annex 4-C register |\n| EWR-F03               | Warning message approval and dissemination log         | Message version, issuer, approval, channel, recipients, acknowledgement, failure and correction.                 | Designated warning/public information focal person  | EOC-WARN-02        |\n| EWR-F04               | PDRA / heightened preparedness coordination record     | Source, impacts, exposure, vulnerability, capacities, assumptions, options, decisions and update.                | CDRRMO / technical offices                          | GOV-F09            |\n| EOC-F01               | EOC activation, scale-up and deactivation record       | Trigger, decision authority, level, scope, activated functions, notification, review, deactivation and handover. | EOC Manager / authorised official                   | EOC-ACT-01         |\n| EOC-F02               | EOC opening and operational readiness checklist        | Facility, safety, comms, roster, equipment, maps, data, shifts and briefing.                                     | EOC Manager / section leads                         | EOC-F02            |\n| EOC-F03               | Initial incident coordination and ICS interface record | Incident, IC/IMT, command post, objectives, liaison, operational period, requests and escalation.                | EOC Manager                                         | EOC-F03            |\n| EOC-F04               | Incident briefing and shift handover                   | Situation, objectives, tasks, risks, requests, decisions, contacts and open issues.                              | Outgoing/incoming section leads                     | EOC-F04            |\n| ER-F01                | Evacuation coordination and monitoring sheet           | Approved decision, affected areas, messages, transport, facility status, aggregate counts and unmet needs.       | CSWDO / barangay / EOC liaison                      | ER-F01             |\n| ER-F02                | Response deployment and safety coordination record     | Requesting authority, task, location, lead agency, check-in, safety, communications and status.                  | Lead response agency / EOC coordination             | ER-F02             |\n| ER-F03                | Shelter/CCCM service coordination summary              | Facility, aggregate occupancy, services, accessibility, issues, referrals and closure.                           | CSWDO / facility manager                            | ER-F03             |\n| ER-F04                | Public information verification and correction log     | Claim, source, verification status, approval, message and feedback.                                              | Public information focal person                     | ER-F04             |\n| EOC-F05               | Situation Report quality and submission register       | Period, cut-off, inputs, verification, approval, recipient, submission and supersession.                         | EOC Planning / records custodian                    | EOC-SITREP-01      |\n| EOC-F06               | Resource request referral and status sheet             | Need, priority, owner, availability, approval route, dispatch, receipt and closeout.                             | EOC Logistics / Chapter 5 interface                 | EOC-F06            |\n| ER-F05                | Demobilisation and transition handover register        | Outstanding tasks, resources, information, receiving office, due date and acknowledgment.                        | EOC Manager / sector leads                          | ER-F05             |\n| ER-F06                | After-action and corrective action record              | Finding, evidence, root/contributing cause, action, owner, deadline, verification and closure.                   | CDRRMO / Chapter 7 interface                        | ER-F06             |\n| Annex 4-A             | IAT and Master Requirements Traceability Register      | Indicator IDs, primary/secondary MR links, process, SOP/form, owner, evidence and validation status.             | CDRRMO MOO custodian                                | Library            |\n| Annex 4-B             | EOC and incident coordination RACI                     | Validated role and approval map for City, EOC, ICS/IMT, clusters and barangays.                                  | CDRRMO / City Legal Office                          | Library            |\n| Annex 4-C             | Hazard-specific warning/activation matrix register     | Controlled matrix index by hazard, source, plan, trigger and approval date.                                      | Operations and Warning / contingency plan custodian | Library            |\n| Annex 4-D             | Gawad KALASAG CY 2026 evidence crosswalk               | Chapter 4 record, toolkit criterion and means of verification.                                                   | CDRRMO MOO custodian                                | Library            |\n\nFive Chapter 4 forms match forms that MODE already had, and records already exist under the MODE codes, so those codes are kept: EWR-F01 is EOC-WARN-01, EWR-F03 is EOC-WARN-02, EWR-F04 is GOV-F09 (Annex 1-G), EOC-F01 is EOC-ACT-01 and EOC-F05 is EOC-SITREP-01. The other forms are loaded in MODE under their Chapter 4 codes. EWR-F02 is a controlled register, not a step form.\n\n# 19. Relationship with the Succeeding Chapters\n\n**Table 4.38**\n\n*Interfaces With the Other Chapters*\n\n| **Chapter** | **Subject**                                                                      | **Chapter 4 interface**                                                                                                                                                                          |\n|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1           | Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability                  | Provides statutory/administrative decision rights, CDRRMC/Mayor routes, State of Calamity and State of Imminent Disaster distinctions, EOC establishment proposal and ICS boundary.              |\n| 2           | CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and Human Resource Management          | Provides permanent CDRRMO functions, duty system, EOC staffing, alternates, competency and duty-of-care requirements.                                                                            |\n| 3           | Risk Intelligence, DRRM and Contingency Planning, and Institutional Preparedness | Provides authoritative data, CDRA, scenarios, contingency plans, PSCP, barangay planning and inclusion requirements.                                                                             |\n| 5           | DRRM Financing, Procurement and Resource Accountability                          | Owns financing, procurement, expenditure, property, LDRRMF and audit controls; Chapter 4 identifies and coordinates operational needs only.                                                      |\n| 6           | EOC Operations, Information Management, Logistics and Coordination               | Owns detailed EOC facility/operations, communications, common operating picture, data/GIS, logistics and coordination procedures; Chapter 4 provides activation and incident management context. |\n| 7           | Monitoring, Evaluation, Knowledge Management and Continuous Improvement          | Owns performance framework, records review, knowledge management, after-action learning and corrective-action monitoring.                                                                        |\n| 8           | Recovery, Rehabilitation and Build Back Better                                   | Receives the incident transition, damage/needs information, outstanding recovery priorities and sector handover.                                                                                 |\n| 9           | Partnerships, Local Ownership and Institutional Sustainability                   | Provides partnership, mutual aid, CSO/private-sector, volunteer and local ownership arrangements used in readiness and response.                                                                 |\n\n# 20. Conclusion\n\nChapter 4 establishes the operational chain that connects authoritative warnings and verified local observations with timely decisions, risk communication, EOC activation, ICS-supported incident management, emergency response coordination and transition. Its central control is clarity: the source of information is identifiable; technical meaning is preserved; each decision is made by the competent authority; each task has a responsible office; the EOC supports rather than commands field operations; and each action can be traced through an operational record.\n\nThe chapter is not implemented merely because these procedures are written. Institutionalisation requires valid local EOC and ICS issuances, hazard-specific warning-action matrices, current source and contact registers, named staff and alternates, accessible communication channels, exercised EOC/ICS interfaces, reliable reporting, secure and complete records, and corrective actions verified by the responsible offices. Until these controls are approved, tested and evidenced, this chapter remains a controlled working draft.\n\n# REFERENCES\n\n- City Government of Ormoc, City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office. (2026). *CDRRMO reference: Local policies* [Shared Drive folder of the City''s DRRM policy instruments: Sangguniang Panlungsod ordinances, executive orders, CDRRMC resolutions and SP resolutions]. https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12NWwUTAE6ub1vW31M2NSMktYlP-BP4oR\n\n- City Government of Ormoc, Sangguniang Panlungsod. (1993–2025). *SP ordinances* [Shared Drive folder, by year, including Ordinance No. 008, s. 2014 establishing the CDRRMO and Ordinance No. 011, s. 2015 amending it]. https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/132g-VeSpXkorcNCte2fpyVY3Az3baBXS\n\n- City Government of Ormoc. (2026). Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC Institutional Assessment Tool (v1.7, 11 November 2026). Unpublished assessment workbook. Repository source: reference/Ormoc_CDRRMO-EOC_Institutional_Assessment_Tool_v1-7.xlsx.\n\n- City Government of Ormoc. (2026). Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC Master Requirements Traceability and 140-Indicator Data Dictionary (v1.1). Unpublished project reference workbook.\n\n- City Government of Ormoc. (2026). Ormoc City CDRRMO–EOC Manual of Operations, Chapter 1: Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability (Draft 1.2, 6 November 2026).\n\n- City Government of Ormoc. (2026). Ormoc City CDRRMO–EOC Manual of Operations, Chapter 2: CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and Human Resource Management (Draft 1.2, 6 November 2026).\n\n- City Government of Ormoc. (2026). Ormoc City CDRRMO–EOC Manual of Operations, Chapter 3: Risk Intelligence, DRRM and Contingency Planning, and Institutional Preparedness (Working Draft 1.1, 8 November 2026).\n\n- National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2012). Memorandum Circular No. 4, s. 2012: Institutionalization of the Incident Command System (ICS) in the Philippines.\n\n- National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2018). Memorandum No. 131, s. 2018: Guidelines on the establishment, operationalization and management of Emergency Operations Center (provisions to be confirmed against a certified copy).\n\n- Republic Act No. 7160. (1991). Local Government Code of 1991.\n\n- Republic Act No. 10121. (2010). Philippine Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Act of 2010.\n\n- Republic Act No. 10173. (2012). Data Privacy Act of 2012.\n\n- Republic Act No. 12287. (2025). Declaration of State of Imminent Disaster Act, and its 2026 Implementing Rules and Regulations.\n\n- Republic Act No. 12076. (2024). Ligtas Pinoy Centers Act.\n\n- City Government of Ormoc. (2026). Ormoc City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office organizational structure \\[Organizational chart\\]. Positions used; personal names omitted.\n\n- Department of Social Welfare and Development, Department of the Interior and Local Government, Department of Health, & Department of Education. (2021). Joint Memorandum Circular No. 2, s. 2021: Guidelines on camp coordination and camp management and internally displaced persons protection.\n\n- Department of the Interior and Local Government Region VIII. (2025, February 26). Adopting/approving the disaster response reporting template and standard operating procedures for adoption of the local disaster risk reduction and management councils (Memorandum R08-LGCDD-2025-02-26-008), adopting RDRRMC VIII Resolution No. 12-006, s. 2023.\n\n- International Organization for Migration. (n.d.). Camp coordination and camp management (CCCM). In IOM Emergency Manual.\n\n- National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council & Office of Civil Defense. (2020). Contingency planning guidebook (as of February 2020).\n\n- National Economic and Development Authority. (n.d.). Disaster rehabilitation and recovery planning guide.\n\n- Office of Civil Defense. (2026). Gawad KALASAG local DRRM council and office assessment toolkit, CY 2026 \\[Assessment workbook\\].\n\n- Emergency Operations Center capability assessment checklist. (2017, December). Used for the EOC readiness items cross-referenced to Chapter 6.\n\n- Relevant official hazard bulletins, advisories and technical products issued by PAGASA, DOST-PHIVOLCS, DENR-MGB and other competent agencies. Each operational use shall retain the actual product identifier, date and issuing source.\n\n# VALIDATION AND SOURCE CONTROL REGISTER\n\n**Table 4.39**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Validation item**              | **Required action before approval**                                                                                                                                                                                   | **Responsible institution / reviewer** |\n|----------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|\n| IAT v1.7 A6/A7/A8/B1.2–B1.5      | Rows reconciled and copied into Annex 4-A (8 November 2026). Validate scores and evidence at the December 2026 workshop; all 29 rows are "Pending validation" in the workbook.                                        | CDRRMO / assessment team               |\n| MR-01–MR-18 mapping              | Functional MR links taken from the indicator-to-MR table of the Data Dictionary (Annex 4-A). Confirm the primary MR for indicators linked to more than one functional area.                                           | CDRRMO / platform data custodian       |\n| EOC establishment / CONOPS       | Verify EOC EO, activation authority, OpCen transition, alternate EOC and reporting route.                                                                                                                             | Mayor / CLO / CDRRMO / OCD VIII        |\n| NDRRMC Memo 131 (2018)           | Scanned project copy holds the title; obtain a certified copy and verify the operative provisions.                                                                                                                    | OCD VIII / CDRRMO                      |\n| ICS–EOC boundary                 | Validate ICS EO, IC/IMT, EOC Manager, clusters and incident command appointments.                                                                                                                                     | OCD VIII / CLO / agencies              |\n| Warning-action thresholds        | Validate each hazard trigger against current official products and approved contingency plans.                                                                                                                        | Source agencies / CDRRMO / sectors     |\n| Evacuation authority / protocols | Reconcile ordinance, decision-makers, suspensions and barangay implementation.                                                                                                                                        | CLO / Mayor / CDRRMC / CSWDO           |\n| Regional reports / cut-offs      | Obtained: DILG VIII Memorandum R08-LGCDD-2025-02-26-008 (26 Feb 2025), RDRRMC VIII Res. No. 12-006 s. 2023. Confirm it is still the current version and confirm the provincial recipient.                             | DILG VIII / OCD VIII / CDRRMO          |\n| Scenario modules / staffing      | Validate roster, alternates, cluster desks, shifts, welfare and minimum coverage.                                                                                                                                     | HRMO / CDRRMO / partners               |\n| Digital records / privacy        | Verify role controls, audit, retention, offline behaviour and sensitive-data safeguards.                                                       